# The branch that claims a task is named for its id and the file that describes
# it is named for its id, so the two names are one name. A file where they part
# is a task that cannot be looked up from a branch or from a dependency that
# names it.
run available
exit 3
file tasks/M1-07.md
	---
	id: M1-06
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
stderr
	tasks.sh: tasks/M1-07.md: frontmatter says id M1-06, and a task file is named for the id it carries
